# Plans

This section tracks design and delivery plans for work that changes how the service is built, or that produces components other services may reuse.

A plan must be reviewed and marked **Approved** before the work it describes is integrated into any new front end.

## How to add a plan

1. Create a page in `docs/source/documentation/plans/` named after the work, for example `eligibility-journey.html.md.erb`.
2. Set `last_reviewed_on` and `review_in` in the front matter.
3. Start the page with a status table: status, author, reviewers, last updated.
4. Add a row to the register below.
5. Raise a pull request so the plan is reviewed like code. Record decisions made in review in the plan's decision log.

## Statuses

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Draft | Being written, not ready for review |
| In review | Open for comment in a pull request |
| Approved | Agreed; work can be integrated |
| Superseded | Replaced by a later plan (link to it) |
| Abandoned | Not going ahead (record why) |

